<title>USA: Total U.S. copper stocks up in November - ABMS.</title>
<headline>Total U.S. copper stocks up in November - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total copper stocks held by U.S. rod mills and refiners (including wirebars, cathodes, scrap, rod and in-process material) rose by the end of November to an estimated 137,422,000 lbs from an estimated October tally of 125,402,000 lbs, the American Bureau of Metal Statistics said.</p>
<p>Rod stocks held by refiners and rod mills rose to an estimated 61,241,000 lbs from an estimated 48,837,000 lbs in October.</p>
<p>Cathode inventories at rod mills fell to an estimated 64,006,000 lbs in November from an estimated 66,506,000 the previous month.</p>
<p>	  --New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1640</p>
